  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthen the Capacity of Colombian Institutions to Develop Strategies to Promote Peacebuilding, Security, and Reconciliation for the Stabilization of Territories and the Benefit of Civil Society Organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project&#x2019;s objective is &#x201C; Contribute to peacebuilding, security, and reconciliation, promoting the stabilization conditions in the prioritized territories in Colombia&#x201D;. Specifically, the project will seek to develop and strengthen innovative peacebuilding, security and reconciliation strategies formulated by national and local level entities that are responsible for implementing peace and territorial stabilization policies. In this way, state institutions and civil society organizations will be able to strengthen their capacities to develop and implement actions related to the framework of the peace policies, with special emphasis on victims&#x2019; rights and providing security conditions for those in the most vulnerable situations. This includes reducing the risks for communities affected by illicit conflict economies and organize crime, which produce not only displacement processes caused by the conflict and environmental degradation but also damage to the social and community structures of vulnerable and conflict-affected populations. Moreover, the project seeks to generate strengthened actions that promote the mobilization of strategic lines within the National Development Plan 2022-2026, in which refers to the fulfillment of the transformations and catalytic actions that involve the implementation of the Four-Year Plan of the Peace Agreement, its articulation with the Total Peace Policy and the necessary cross-cutting differential perspective.</narrative>
  </description>
